# Split-section image side

If a section is **heading + paragraph(s) + CTA**, it is **P-03** (`Content.astro`). Always include a side image. Do not use P-13 for this shape.

## Which side

Inspect the page top to bottom. Find the **nearest previous split** (any section that already has a left/right image: P-01 `Hero2`, P-03 `Content`, P-08 with an image). Put this section's image on the **opposite** side.

How to read a split:

| Component | Image RIGHT (text left) | Image LEFT (text right) |
|---|---|---|
| `Hero2` | Default (always) | — |
| `Content` / `Steps` | No `isReversed` | `isReversed` |

Typical page: Hero image is on the **right**, so the next P-03 uses `isReversed` (image **left**). The one after that is default (image **right**). Keep flipping.

Skip cards, stats, FAQ, testimonials, P-12, P-13, and other full-width blocks — they do not change the next image side.

If this is the first split on the page, default to image **right** (text left), then alternate from there.

If the brief has no image URL, still add the image slot with a relevant photo and accurate alt text. Never drop the image to "save" a heading+para+CTA section.
